L120:  | $$\delta(k)=\frac{I\left(\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}_{(k)};Y\right)-I\left(\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}_{(k-1)};Y\right)}{I(\mathcal{X}^{\prime}_{Q};Y)},$$  |  | (4)
L121: 
L122: and stop when $\delta(k)>\bar{\delta}$.
L123: 
L124:  | $\displaystyle I(\mathcal{X}^{\prime}_{Q};Y)=\sum_{x^{\prime}}p(x^{\prime})\sum_{y}p(y\!\mid\!x^{\prime})\,\log\frac{p(y\!\mid\!x^{\prime})}{p(y)}.$  |  | (5)
L125: IB requires the conditional $p(y\mid x^{\prime})$ that quantifies the task-relevance of each primitive $x^{\prime}\in\mathcal{X}^{\prime}_{Q}$. The cosine similarity function $\varphi(\cdot,\cdot)$ measures how well a primitive ($f_{x’}$) aligns with a task cue ($f_{t}$), serving as a semantic relevance score.
